# Research Wiki Maintenance

**Constitution guardrails:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) §6 · Wiki is **navigation**, not behavior truth.

## Read before substantial work

Research, labeling, review tooling, or non-trivial implementation:

- `docs/research_wiki/index.md`
- `docs/research_wiki/handoff.md`
- `docs/research_wiki/log.md` (tail)

Truth: source docs, code, labels, experiment outputs, GitHub issues. When wiki and
evidence disagree, **source wins** — fix or flag the wiki
([source-authority.md](../../docs/research_wiki/reference/source-authority.md)).

## Update after meaningful work

Before final response when durable context was created:

- Smallest relevant page under `docs/research_wiki/`
- `index.md` if pages added/moved/retired
- One append to `log.md`
- `handoff.md` if focus, next action, blockers, or verification changed

Skip for trivial Q&A, status-only replies, or mechanical changes with no research context.

## Guardrails

- Link to source docs; do not copy long specs into wiki.
- Stay within repo doc bounds.
- No promoting wiki notes to runtime behavior.
- No auto-fib, trading signals, edge claims, ML loops, or optimization via wiki.
- `*_candidate` ≠ human facit.
